    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW257Mdet5dXQHZmdGYA1j39j)_\n\n## Problem\nAt launch a `*scratch*` window opens beside the Dashboard instead of the Dashboard alone.\n\n## Likely cause\nSince 8e1917b (Oct 23) `tabspaces-mode` starts after init with `tabspaces-session-auto-restore`. On startup it restores the window layout saved at the last exit (`window-state-put`). `sp-dashboard--setup-splash-hooks` runs later, on `window-setup-hook`, and only replaces the buffer of the selected window, so any restored second window (here `*scratch*`) stays. The layout is saved again at every exit, so it keeps coming back. Nothing in the PRs #114-#131 touches this (quick-capture #131 is not merged).\n\n## Fix\n`sp-dashboard--setup-splash-hooks` calls `delete-other-windows` before drawing the Dashboard. It runs once at start-up only, not on refresh. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not verified\nNot run in Emacs (none in the sandbox); the cause is from reading the config and the upstream `tabspaces` source. Please check in a fresh Emacs. If `*scratch*` still appears, `M-: (window-list)` right after launch and the contents of `var/tabspaces-session.eld` would show who creates it. Under `emacs --daemon` tabspaces defers the restore to the first client frame, which runs after this hook, so a daemon setup could still show the split.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01EA37EZhazyp5aMzFJXxDqR)_",
